{"id": "EUVD-2026-86183", "enisaUuid": "1ee778cd-bd9c-32b3-85ab-6bf907abe33d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: pcie: null RX pointers after free\n\nWhen iwl_pcie_tx_init() fails after RX init, nic init unwinds via\niwl_pcie_rx_free().\n\nThe freed RX members stayed non-NULL on the live transport object,\nso later teardown or retry could touch stale RX state.\nSet rx_pool, global_table, rxq, and alloc_page to NULL after free\nto make repeated cleanup and retry paths safe.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:37", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c422d5d53f135ea987f745773953a91f9fe30c3f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ec5bf430cf7466cb412e47f2761594092781fac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3456c5bcc987aeb182e50e30c9b02be8420e9953", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c79d7a7b583050c9f58041465cb46fe3483ab5d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93796", "GHSA-fgmq-vv8f-hphc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0814d803-fc92-3fab-ad7e-83f7639aa0e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cf671d60fdbeb8f875859c11148cf13c326ada2 <6ec5bf430cf7466cb412e47f2761594092781fac"}, {"id": "34fd599c-772c-3b05-9f3e-e81ca1afc9ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "51533133-99d9-3b30-a641-3c3566dc6912", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6b58d520-8241-3e04-9363-0604e1d9efc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "6c58a68d-749a-37ad-91bc-63716243edaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cf671d60fdbeb8f875859c11148cf13c326ada2 <3456c5bcc987aeb182e50e30c9b02be8420e9